{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"n1","type":"text","text":"# SIGNAL — RELEASE CONTROL\n\n## Podcast Guest Consent & Excerpt Withdrawal\n\nA service-oriented platform for excerpt-level consent management, auditable withdrawal, and producer-managed distribution removal tasks.\n\n**Core principle:** withdrawing one excerpt must not affect sibling excerpts.","x":500,"y":-500,"width":700,"height":220,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"n3","type":"text","text":"## FRONTEND\n\n`web-dashboard`\n\n- Guest portal\n- Producer portal\n- Excerpt request forms\n- Consent management\n- Distribution task tracking\n- Notifications\n\nCommunicates through API Gateway.\n\nPublic API: `localhost:8080`","x":325,"y":-200,"width":350,"height":280,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"n5","type":"text","text":"## SERVICE DISCOVERY\n\n**Eureka**\n\n`discovery-server`\n\nRegisters Spring applications and supports service discovery.\n\nActuator health endpoints support Docker Compose health checks.","x":2000,"y":-200,"width":350,"height":280,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"n2","type":"text","text":"## USERS\n\n**GUEST**\n- Request excerpts\n- View own releases and consent scopes\n- Withdraw consent\n- Track removal tasks\n- View notifications\n\n**PRODUCER**\n- Create episodes and excerpts\n- Review guest requests\n- Grant releases\n- Manage removal tasks","x":-525,"y":-200,"width":350,"height":280,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"n4","type":"text","text":"## SECURITY & GATEWAY\n\n**Keycloak**\n- Realm: `podcast-demo`\n- Client: `podcast-dashboard`\n- Roles: `guest`, `podcastProducer`\n- JWT authentication\n\n**Spring Cloud Gateway**\n- API routing\n- JWT validation\n- Role checks\n- Correlation IDs\n\nServices also verify record ownership.","x":1125,"y":-200,"width":400,"height":440,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"n6","type":"text","text":"## MICROSERVICES\n\n**podcast-excerpt-service**\n- Episodes and excerpts\n- Guest excerpt requests\n- Producer approval/rejection\n- In-app notifications\n- Database: `excerpt_db`\n\n**guest-release-service**\n- Releases and consent scopes\n- Withdrawal decisions\n- Audit and transactional outbox\n- Database: `release_db`\n\n**distribution-task-service**\n- Kafka consumer\n- Idempotency\n- Removal task management\n- Database: `distribution_db`\n\nEach service owns its database.","x":-625,"y":604,"width":450,"height":644,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"n12","type":"text","text":"## DATABASE OWNERSHIP\n\n**excerpt_db**\n- Episodes\n- Excerpts\n- Excerpt requests\n- Notifications\n\n**release_db**\n- guest_release\n- release_scope\n- release_audit\n- event_outbox\n- Ownership/reference projections\n\n**distribution_db**\n- distribution_task\n- processed_event\n- Distributed edit graph\n- Guest/episode projections\n\nFlyway migrations. No cross-service foreign keys.","x":-625,"y":2008,"width":450,"height":632,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"n7","type":"text","text":"## EXCERPT REQUEST WORKFLOW\n\n1. Guest selects a published episode.\n2. Guest submits timestamps, title and description.\n3. Request is stored as `PENDING`.\n4. Producer reviews the request.\n5. Producer approves or rejects.\n6. Approval creates the excerpt through the existing excerpt domain service.\n7. Guest receives a notification.\n\n**Important:** approval does not automatically grant consent. A release must be granted separately.","x":1245,"y":604,"width":420,"height":436,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"n10","type":"text","text":"## DISTRIBUTION EVENT CONSUMER\n\n`distribution-task-service`\n\n1. Consumes `GuestExcerptWithdrawn`.\n2. Validates guest and episode projection.\n3. Begins transaction in `distribution_db`.\n4. Claims event in `processed_event` using `ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING`.\n5. Duplicate event: rollback and acknowledge.\n6. First delivery: find distributed edits containing the excerpt.\n7. Create one removal task per matching edit.\n8. Commit event claim and tasks atomically.\n\nUnique task identity:\n`(event_id, edit_id)`\n\nProcessing is idempotent; Kafka delivery is at least once.","x":1855,"y":1858,"width":550,"height":400,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"n13","type":"text","text":"## RELIABILITY & CONSISTENCY\n\n- Scope update + outbox insert are atomic.\n- Kafka delivery is at least once.\n- Consumer claim + task writes are atomic.\n- Duplicate events are handled idempotently.\n- Unique scope: `(release_id, excerpt_id)`.\n- Unique outbox: `(aggregate_id, event_type)`.\n- Unique task: `(event_id, edit_id)`.\n- Correlation ID follows HTTP and Kafka.\n\nNo claim of end-to-end exactly-once processing.","x":825,"y":2385,"width":420,"height":375,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"n11","type":"text","text":"## TASK LIFECYCLE\n\n`OPEN`\n\n↓\n\n`IN_PROGRESS`\n\n↓\n\n`DONE`\n\nProducer can attach:\n- Notes\n- Evidence URL\n- Completion details\n\nSystem records updater and timestamps.\n\nGuests can view their own tasks but cannot update them.\n\n**DONE is a recorded producer action, not proof of an external platform API call.**","x":2820,"y":2410,"width":380,"height":590,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"n15","type":"text","text":"## PRESENTATION TAKEAWAY\n\n**Signal turns excerpt-level consent withdrawal into an auditable, asynchronous operational workflow.**\n\nIt preserves sibling consent, records withdrawal transactionally, propagates the event through Kafka, prevents duplicate task creation, and gives producers trackable removal work.\n\nThe demo coordinates and records removal tasks. It does not automatically delete content from Spotify, TikTok or YouTube.","x":1640,"y":3210,"width":1100,"height":230,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"n14","type":"text","text":"## DEMO FAN-OUT\n\nTarget excerpt:\n`ex-ava-020500`\n\nMatching distributed edits:\n- YouTube\n- Spotify\n- TikTok\n\nResult: **3 removal tasks**.\n\nSocial and Website are unaffected because they do not contain the target excerpt.\n\nControl excerpt:\n`ex-ava-341000`\n\nRemains `ACTIVE` with zero tasks.","x":3720,"y":2410,"width":380,"height":470,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"n9","type":"text","text":"## KAFKA\n\nWithdrawal event topic:\n\n`soa.s14.t04.events`\n\n- Durable event transport\n- Outbox publishing\n- Asynchronous consumer\n- Retry with exponential backoff\n- Dead-letter topic:\n  `soa.s14.t04.events.DLT`\n\nNotification topic:\n\n`soa.s14.t04.notifications`","x":1940,"y":1282,"width":380,"height":432,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"n8","type":"text","text":"## CONSENT WITHDRAWAL SEQUENCE\n\n1. Guest authenticates through Keycloak.\n2. Guest receives a JWT access token.\n3. Guest calls:\n\n`POST /api/releases/{releaseId}/scopes/{excerptId}/withdrawals`\n\n4. Gateway validates JWT, role and correlation ID.\n5. Release service checks ownership and scope.\n6. One database transaction:\n   - Set the selected scope to `WITHDRAWN`.\n   - Record actor, timestamp and reason.\n   - Preserve sibling scopes.\n   - Withdraw parent release only if no active scopes remain.\n   - Insert event into outbox.\n7. API returns `202 Accepted` with event ID.\n8. Outbox publisher sends event to Kafka.\n\n**The withdrawal is recorded before asynchronous distribution processing.**","x":825,"y":1248,"width":550,"height":592,"color":"4"}
	],
